{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Fix pushed for review: Gerrit change 1357 (https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/1357), commit c08873d0c70.\n\nChange: .claude/settings.json hook command anchored as \"$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR\"/scripts/hooks/serena_grep_reminder.py. Guard tests added to tests/unit/test_serena_grep_reminder_hook.py: (1) test_no_hook_command_uses_a_relative_path — static guard covering every hook entry in the file (AC2); (2) test_hook_command_resolves_from_a_foreign_cwd — runs the exact configured command via /bin/sh from a cwd without scripts/ and asserts exit 0 + the reminder JSON (AC1/AC4 mechanism).\n\nRED→GREEN evidence: both tests seen failing against the relative path (AssertionError on the relative command; exit 127 'No such file or directory'), green after the fix; mutation check (git stash of the settings fix) returned both to RED, then restored. Full hook+settings test files: 38 passed. make lint clean.\n\nManual replication of the original report: configured command piped the grep envelope from cwd=.tickets-tracker with CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR set → additionalContext emitted, exit 0 (was exit 127 before).\n\nSibling sweep: .claude/settings.json contains exactly one hook entry; no other tracked config executes a hook command (checked git grep '\"command\"' over *.json — only docs experiment records and a JSON schema). Awaiting LLM-Review/Verified votes."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785857532701842001,"uuid":"58209b0f-3dd3-470e-8220-51e67d64ca4d"}